 "definition": "cov/coverage.py (10-20, spec \u00a74.102 item 4): empirical coverage of the deviation margin lambda_l * sigma_hat_l.\nRead-only use of the frozen qsim code: sigma_hat comes from v8sim2.Prior built on prior_traces.json with\nv8sim7.cfg_measured() (the configuration v8sim10.sim_nest2 / the daemon use), kind \"win\" (replenishment).\n\nRise definition = exactly Prior's \"win\" sample (v8sim2.py:39-42; same as export_sigma.py -> daemon prior_sigma.json):\n    R(t) = max(0, max_{tau in [h0, h0+g]} D(t+tau) - D(t)),  g = TICK = 30 s,\n    h0 = h_UP = 30 s (UP), h_VY = 150 s (VY), h_WK + h_UP = 150 s (WK); i.e. the arrival window [H-g, H] of the\n    replenish horizon H = cfg.win = 60 / 180 / 180 s. This is NOT the max over (0, H] (that is Prior's \"run\" kind);\n    the full-horizon max (0, H] is reported as a secondary, stricter column.\nMargin  M(t) = lambda_l * Prior.sigma(\"win\", l, D(t)) (bucket 10 UE, linear interpolation between bucket centres).\nUnits: UE (40-UE scale). The daemon multiplies both D and sigma by ue_pps = 250 kpps; R > M is invariant to that factor.\nEvaluation points: each minute start t = 0..59 min whose arrival window lies inside the 60-min trace\n(primary, as requested), and every 30-s planner tick (the exact sample set Prior was fitted on; secondary).\nIn-sample: sigma_hat is fitted on the same 1615 traces.\n",
